                <pb facs="1068" n="1008" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg1008"/>

                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">UNITED STATES OF COLOMBIA—COMMANDING GENERAL OF MARINE AND OF
                    THE SECOND DIVISION OF THE COLOMBIAN GUARD—NO. 98.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">To the Governor of the Province of Baranquilla</hi>:</p>
                <p>At 4½ p. m., this day, after a fight of thirty minutes, the troops under my
                    command occupied this city, (Banco.)</p>
                <p>A detailed report of the action will he sent to you in due time; I now give
                    generalities.</p>
                <p>We have captured Manuel A. Vengorchea, acting President of Magdalena, four
                    chiefs, fourteen officers, thirty-nine men, and all the munitions of the
                    enemy.</p>
                <pb facs="1069" n="1009" xml:id="pg1009"/>
                <p>We had ten men killed and three wounded; most of them belonged to the regenerator
                    battalion.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. LOPEZ.</signed>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Banco,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 28, 1867</date>, <hi rendition="#italic">on board the
                            steamer Vencedor.</hi></dateline>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>J. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pinzon</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rico</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                            Secretary.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
